'''Ampurias''' ({{IPA-bl|əmˈpuɾiəs}}; from {{Langx|el|Ἐμπόριον|Emporion|trading place}}) is a [[Boroughs of Castejón|borough]] and {{W|urban enterprise zone}} of the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. It is bordered to the northeast by the [[Expansión]] borough, and is bounded by [[Salto Bay]] on the remaining three sides. It is the smallest borough by area and the eleventh-most populous, with a population of 832,879 in the [[2025 Baliscan census]]. Ampurias has been described as the most prominent cultural, financial, media, and entertainment center in Balisca. 

The borough hosts the headquarters of various {{W|international organization}}s along with major domestic [[W:Cooperative|cooperatives]] such as the [[Castejón Broadcasting Collective]], and the [[Rinaldi Co-op]]. Due to its special economic status, it is the area where many {{W|multinational corporations}} and other corporations have their regional headquarters.

